s enterprise resource planning (ERP) platforms, directly with Absa\u2019s infrastructure."),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](8,"p"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](9,"Aligned with the evolving payments and collections landscape, as guided by the central bank, a new service called PayShap Request has been introduced within the Collections domain. Leveraging the existing API infrastructure, "),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](10,"b"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](11,"PayShap Request"),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275text"](12," provides both retail and corporate customers with an additional method for initiating collections and payments, which offers near-instantaneous settlement."),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](13,"h1"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](14,"Benefits"),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](15,"p"),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](16,"b"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](17,"Secure messaging framework"),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](18,"ul"),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](19,"li"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](20," PayShap Request operates as a secure messaging layer over existing payment infrastructures (e.g. Faster Payments and the Cards Network). "),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](21,"li"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](22," It facilitates communication between payers and payees without being a payment instrument itself. "),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](23,"p"),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](24,"b"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](25,"Real-time interaction"),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](26,"ul"),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](27,"li"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](28," PayShap Request enables near-instantaneous initiation and response to payment requests. "),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](29,"li"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](30," It supports both immediate and deferred acceptance and payment actions. "),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](31,"p"),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](32,"b"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](33,"Open API integration"),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](34,"ul"),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](35,"li"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](36," PayShap Request services are typically built on Open Banking APIs, which allows seamless integration with banking apps and ERP systems. "),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](37,"li"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](38," This supports automation and scalability for corporate and retail use cases. "),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](39,"p"),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](40,"b"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](41,"Enhanced control and transparency"),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](42,"ul"),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](43,"li"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](44," Payers have more control over when and how they pay. "),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](45,"li"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](46," Billers gain visibility into payment status and customer responses. "),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](47,"li"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](48," Users benefit from improved reconciliation. "),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](49,"li"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](50," PayShap Request frameworks often include features like unique reference numbers and structured messaging to simplify reconciliation for businesses. "),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](51,"p"),r["\u0275\u0275elementStart"](52,"b"),r["\u0275\u0275text"](53,"Payment options for payers"),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275elementEnd"](),r["\u0275\u0275el